# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as-is.
#
# This matters for more than tidiness: tools/hooks/pre-push is a shell script run
# by the sh that ships with Git for Windows. Checked out with CRLF, its shebang
# line ends in a carriage return and the hook dies with a "bad interpreter"
# error that names an interpreter which plainly does exist.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF or PowerShell can misparse them.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
